<%# One catalogue card, shared by every index.

  The card links to the entry's own page when it has one. TikTok is the single entry that does not: the
  inventory's verdict is "mention only, labelled beta", so it keeps its card, its badge and its prerequisite
  and links nowhere -- which is honest, and still not a dead link.

  THE PREREQUISITE IS THE POINT OF THE CARD, not a footnote on it: "you need a WhatsApp Business account" is
  the sentence that decides whether a reader can use this channel today. It sits on its own tinted strip at
  the foot of the card, where the eye lands last and the answer is waiting.
%>
<article class="group flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-lyn-line bg-lyn-paper transition-colors hover:border-lyn-royal/40">
  <div class="flex grow flex-col p-5">
    <h2 class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-ink">
      <% if entry.detail? %>
        <a class="transition-colors hover:text-lyn-royal" href="<%= marketing_entry_path(scope, entry) %>">
          <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
        </a>
      <% else %>
        <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.name") %>
      <% end %>
      <%= render 'marketing/shared/state_badge', state: entry.state %>
    </h2>

    <p class="mt-2 grow text-sm leading-[1.8] text-lyn-ink-soft">
      <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.summary") %>
    </p>
  </div>

  <% if t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.requires", default: nil).present? %>
    <p class="border-t border-lyn-line bg-lyn-mist px-5 py-3 text-xs leading-[1.75] text-lyn-ink-soft">
      <span class="font-semibold text-lyn-ink">
        <%= t(scope == :channels ? 'marketing.state.you_supply' : 'marketing.state.requires') %>
      </span>
      <%= t("marketing.#{scope}.#{entry.id}.requires") %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
</article>
